# Line endings are *content* in this repo, not formatting.
#
# tests/fixtures/golden.html is compared byte-for-byte by the Stage 0 regression
# gate, and the renderer always emits LF. Git's Windows default
# (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites it to CRLF on checkout, so without this file a
# fresh Windows clone fails its own gate before a line of code is touched.
#
# Stage 2 additionally hashes the shipped templates into
# Templates/.installed.json at first-run copy time to tell "user edited this"
# from "last version's default". Those hashes must be identical on every
# machine, which they are not if checkout rewrites line endings.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts keep CRLF so they behave under any host shell.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# Never touched by end-of-line conversion.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
